 "summary": "The migration deletes the `IsPositiveDefiniteKernel` shadow predicate outright with no alias or forwarding module, and routes every binary operation to Mathlib's `Matrix.PosSemidef` API (`.submatrix`, `.add`, `.smul`, `.hadamard`, `posSemidef_sum`, `diag_nonneg`, `isHermitian.apply`, `posSemidef_is_closed`). The declarations retained in the new `TauCeti/Analysis/Matrix/PosSemidef.lean` are all strictly more general than, or absent from, Mathlib \u2014 its `posSemidef_vecMulVec_star_self` and `posSemidef_gram` require `[Finite n]`, and it has no arbitrary-index quadratic-form characterization or entrywise Cauchy--Schwarz \u2014 and each has in-repository consumers.",
